  <exercise number="395" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>If the function $$f\left( {x,y} \right)$$ and all its second derivatives are continuous everywhere, then $$f_{xy} = f_{yx}.$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>True, by Clairaut’s theorem</p>
    </solution>
