  <exercise number="405" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>$$u\left( {x,y} \right) = x^{4} - 3xy + 1,x = 2t,y = t^{3}$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>$$\frac{\partial u}{\partial x} = 4x^{3} - 3y,\frac{\partial u}{\partial y} = -3x,\frac{dx}{dt} = 2,\frac{dy}{dt} = 3t^{2},\frac{du}{dt} = 40t^{3}$$</p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
