  <exercise number="419" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>A machinist is constructing a right circular cone out of a block of aluminum. The machine gives an error of $$5\text{\%}$$ in height and $$2\text{\%}$$ in radius. Find the maximum error in the volume of the cone if the machinist creates a cone of height $$6$$ cm and radius $$2$$ cm.</p>
